  "name": "cs444-lab5",
  "description": "An implementation of Single-Producer Multiple-Consumer (SPMC) synchronization primitives exploring the trade-offs between locking granularity and performance. The repository includes coarse-grained mutex wrappers, optimized locking structures, and lockless implementations targeting POSIX thread environments. It serves as a pedagogical reference for concurrent data structure design, addressing issues such as busy-waiting, critical section contention, and memory safety in shared-memory systems.",
